    "color": "#10a74a",
    "visibility": "public",
    "description_md": "CTD downcast profiles with temperature, salinity, oxygen, fluorescence, and other sensors at standard depths. 1 m-binned final data for 1993-2002 come from the SIO-CalCOFI Technical Group's own archive (J. Wilkinson), which covers the decade calcofi.org does not publish finals for; 1998 and 2003 onward come from calcofi.org. Where both publish the same cruise, calcofi.org is used; the two agree on 130 of 140 comparable files, and the four cruises that differ are recorded in question calcofi_ctd-cast_20.\n",
    "keywords": ["EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN TEMPERATURE > WATER TEMPERATURE", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > SALINITY/DENSITY > OCEAN SALINITY", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN CHEMISTRY > OXYGEN", "EARTH SCIENCE > OCEANS > OCEAN PRESSURE > WATER PRESSURE", "Temperature", "Salinity", "Dissolved Oxygen", "Dissolved Nutrients", "Phytoplankton Biomass and Diversity", "CalCOFI Network"],
    "display": {
      "name_plain": "Sensor Profiles by Depth: Temperature, Salinity, Oxygen",
      "description_short": "Water-column profiles from the CTD sensors, at 1 m resolution (the bottle database is about 10 to 100 m) — temperature, salinity, dissolved oxygen, fluorescence/chlorophyll-a, nitrate and more.",
      "description_lede": null,
      "notes_md": "The CTD is a Sea-Bird SBE 911plus, surrounded by a rosette of 24 10-liter Niskin bottles. Final 1 m-binned data for 1993–2002 come from the SIO-CalCOFI Technical Group’s own archive (J. Wilkinson), which covers the decade calcofi.org does not publish finals for; 1998 and 2003 onward come from calcofi.org. Where both publish the same cruise, calcofi.org is used.",
      "collection": "CTD sensor package on a 24-bottle rosette, lowered at each CalCOFI station",
      "analysis": "Sensor measurements, binned to 1 m",
      "analysis_org": "CalCOFI",
      "collection_method": {
        "key": "ctd",
        "label": "CTD sensors"
      },
      "collection_status": "ongoing",
      "browse_group": "ctd-bottle",
      "spatial_note": null,
      "references": [
        {
          "label": "CTD-Rosette cast",
          "url": "https://wp.calcofi.org/wp/ctd-rosette-cast/"
        },
        {
          "label": "CTD / Bottle sampling methods",
          "url": "https://wp.calcofi.org/wp/data/sampling-info/methods/bottle-sampling-methods/"
        }
      ],
      "column_notes": {
        "cruise_key": "CalCOFI cruise, as year-month-ship code (YYYY-MM-NODC). Cruise_ID in the original cast file.",
        "data_stage": "final, or preliminary while a cruise’s calibrations are not yet applied.",
        "dataset_key": "calcofi_ctd-cast on every row.",
        "datetime": "Date and time (UTC) of the cast. In CalCOFI’s original cast file (Date, Time), the time is when the CTD reached its terminal depth.",
        "depth_max_m": "Deepest depth of the reading, in metres. The CTD profile is binned to 1 m.",
        "depth_min_m": "Shallowest depth of the reading, in metres. The CTD profile is binned to 1 m.",
        "grid_key": "CalCOFI station grid cell the cast falls in.",
        "latitude": "Observed latitude of the cast, in decimal degrees (Lat_Dec in the original cast file).",
        "line": "CalCOFI line number: the first number of site_key, for example 090.0.",
        "longitude": "Observed longitude of the cast, in decimal degrees (Lon_Dec in the original cast file).",
        "measurement_qual": "The CTD team’s flag for the reading, as published: 0 good, 1 use the primary sensor, 2 use the secondary sensor, 4 below detection limit (reported as 0), 8 questionable, 9 bad or missing. Blank means 0.",
        "measurement_type": "Which CTD quantity the row is, for example temperature_ave, salinity_ave_corr or oxygen_ml_l_ave_cruise_corr. Sensors 1 and 2, their average, cruise- or station-corrected versions, bottle values and sensor-based estimates. Each is described, with its units, in measurement_type.csv.",
        "measurement_value": "The reading, in the units given in the units column. Corrected, averaged and estimated quantities are explained in measurement_type.csv.",
        "obs_id": "Row number of the reading. Renumbered with every release, so do not rely on it across releases.",
        "order_occ": "Order in which the station was occupied on the cruise (Order_Occ in the original cast file).",
        "realm": "env on every row here: physical and chemical measurements, no organisms.",
        "sample_key": "The cast this reading came from, calcofi_ctd-cast:cast:… Joins sample.csv.",
        "sample_type": "What one row of sample.csv is. In this dataset, a CTD cast.",
        "site_key": "CalCOFI line and station of the cast, for example 090.0 060.0 (Sta_ID in the original cast file).",
        "station": "CalCOFI station number along the line: the second number of site_key, for example 060.0.",
        "units": "Units of measurement_value, copied from measurement_type.csv."
      }
    },
